From 433d81cd563158b458f10687c2bc23dd93654e06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:29:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] policy: add P2MR (BIP 360) output type, address and
 relay rules

Give witness v2 programs of 32 bytes their own output type,
TxoutType::WITNESS_V2_P2MR, reported as "witness_v2_p2mr", and their own
destination type, WitnessV2P2MR, encoded as a bech32m address with witness
version 2 (bc1z / tb1z / bcrt1z). Such outputs are standard, and spending
them is subject to the same relay limits as a Taproot script path spend:
annexes are non-standard and, for leaf version 0xc0, witness stack items
are limited to MAX_STANDARD_TAPSCRIPT_STACK_ITEM_SIZE.

SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR joins STANDARD_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS but not
MANDATORY_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS, so a P2MR spend that breaks the rules is
rejected from the mempool without punishing the peer, while blocks
containing it are still rejected once the deployment is active.

There is no wallet support: signing returns false for these outputs and
IsMine never matches them. doc/p2mr.md records the rules, the activation
heights, the naming and the limits of this implementation.
