diff --git a/doc/p2mr.md b/doc/p2mr.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..85324d7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/p2mr.md
@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@
+# P2MR (BIP 360) in this build
+
+This build implements the Pay-to-Merkle-Root (P2MR) spending rules of
+[BIP 360](https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/620871a7a442e276a058b487cd8743775fb499a4/bip-0360.mediawiki)
+(draft v0.12.1, bips commit `620871a7a442e276a058b487cd8743775fb499a4`) on top of Bitcoin Core v31.1.
+
+The scope is the consensus and policy treatment of witness v2 outputs. No post-quantum signature
+algorithm is implemented, no wallet descriptor is added and no signing support exists.
+
+## Output format
+
+A P2MR output is a native SegWit output with witness version 2 and a 32-byte witness program:
+
+```
+OP_2 OP_PUSHBYTES_32 <32-byte script tree Merkle root>
+```
+
+The witness program is the Merkle root of the script tree itself. Unlike BIP 341 there is no
+internal public key and no taproot tweak, so there is no key path spend.
+
+Addresses use bech32m with witness version 2, which yields the `bc1z` / `tb1z` / `bcrt1z` prefixes.
+`Solver` reports the type as `witness_v2_p2mr`; `getaddressinfo`, `validateaddress` and
+`decodescript` report witness version 2 and the program.
+
+## Spending rules
+
+The rules below are enforced by `VerifyWitnessProgram` in `src/script/interpreter.cpp` when
+`SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR` is set. They follow the BIP 360 Script Validation section, which in turn
+mirrors the BIP 341 script path.
+
+Let `q` be the 32-byte witness program.
+
+1. The witness stack must have two or more elements.
+2. If the stack has exactly two elements and the first byte of the last one is `0x50`, the spend
+   fails. With three or more elements, a last element starting with `0x50` is the annex: it is
+   removed from the stack, covered by the signature and counted in the transaction weight, but is
+   otherwise ignored. Annexes are non-standard.
+3. The last remaining element is the control block `c`, and the one before it is the script `s`.
+4. `c` must be `1 + 32*m` bytes long, for `m` between 0 and 128 inclusive. The upper bound is 4097
+   bytes (`P2MR_CONTROL_MAX_SIZE`).
+5. The last bit of `c[0]` must be 1. P2MR has no internal key parity to encode, so this bit is
+   unused and is checked for every leaf version, not only for `0xc0`. Failure yields
+   `SCRIPT_ERR_P2MR_WRONG_CONTROL_PARITY`.
+6. The leaf version is `v = c[0] & 0xfe`. The tapleaf hash and the Merkle path folding are exactly
+   those of BIP 341, computed by `ComputeTapleafHash` and `ComputeTapbranchHash`.
+7. The resulting root `r` must equal `q`, otherwise the spend fails. No tweak is applied and no
+   internal public key is parsed.
+8. If `m = 0` the spend succeeds immediately and the script is **not** executed. Such an output is
+   spendable by anyone who learns `v` and `s`, so tools must not produce depth-zero P2MR outputs.
+9. Otherwise, for leaf version `0xc0` the script is executed under the BIP 342 rules, with the
+   tapleaf hash and annex recorded in the script execution data. `OP_SUCCESSx` keeps its BIP 342
+   meaning.
+10. For any other leaf version the spend succeeds without executing the script.
+    `SCRIPT_VERIFY_DISCOURAGE_UPGRADABLE_TAPROOT_VERSION` makes this non-standard, so such spends
+    are rejected by the mempool but accepted in blocks.
+11. The signature message is the BIP 342 common signature message, unchanged. It commits to the
+    actual `OP_2 <root>` scriptPubKey through the spent scripts hash.
+
+P2SH-wrapped witness v2 programs are not P2MR; they keep the unknown witness program behaviour.
+
+## Activation
+
+P2MR is a buried deployment, `Consensus::DEPLOYMENT_P2MR`, with the height parameter
+`consensus.P2MRHeight`:
+
+| Chain | Activation height |
+| --- | --- |
+| mainnet | never (`std::numeric_limits<int>::max()`) |
+| testnet3 | never |
+| testnet4 | never |
+| signet, default challenge | never |
+| signet, custom challenge (`-signetchallenge`) | 1 |
+| regtest | 0, overridable with `-testactivationheight=p2mr@N` |
+
+`GetBlockScriptFlags` sets `SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR` from the activation height onwards, so block
+validation only enforces these rules on chains where the deployment is enabled. When the deployment
+is enabled, the node logs `P2MR consensus rules active from height N` at startup, and
+`getdeploymentinfo` reports a `p2mr` buried deployment.
+
+`SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR` is part of `STANDARD_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS` but not of
+`MANDATORY_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS`. The mempool therefore applies these rules on every chain, including
+the ones where the deployment never activates: a P2MR spend that breaks them is rejected as
+`mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (<script error>)` with result `TX_NOT_STANDARD`, and a block
+containing it is rejected as `block-script-verify-flag-failed (<script error>)` once the deployment
+is active. Script check failures never disconnect or ban a peer.
+
+Relay policy for P2MR spends matches Taproot script path spends: witness stack items are limited to
+`MAX_STANDARD_TAPSCRIPT_STACK_ITEM_SIZE` (80 bytes) for leaf version `0xc0`, and annexes are
+non-standard.
+
+## Naming
+
+| Item | Name |
+| --- | --- |
+| Script verification flag | `SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR`, test name `P2MR` |
+| Deployment | `Consensus::DEPLOYMENT_P2MR`, height `P2MRHeight`, argument name `p2mr` |
+| Output type | `TxoutType::WITNESS_V2_P2MR`, RPC string `witness_v2_p2mr` |
+| Destination type | `WitnessV2P2MR` |
+| Script predicate | `CScript::IsPayToMerkleRoot()` |
+| Constants | `WITNESS_V2_P2MR_SIZE`, `P2MR_CONTROL_BASE_SIZE`, `P2MR_CONTROL_NODE_SIZE`, `P2MR_CONTROL_MAX_NODE_COUNT`, `P2MR_CONTROL_MAX_SIZE` |
+| New script error | `SCRIPT_ERR_P2MR_WRONG_CONTROL_PARITY` |
+
+All other failures reuse existing script errors: `SCRIPT_ERR_WITNESS_PROGRAM_WITNESS_EMPTY`,
+`SCRIPT_ERR_TAPROOT_WRONG_CONTROL_SIZE`, `SCRIPT_ERR_WITNESS_PROGRAM_MISMATCH` and
+`SCRIPT_ERR_DISCOURAGE_UPGRADABLE_TAPROOT_VERSION`.
+
+## Limits of this implementation
+
+- BIP 360 is a draft. This build follows one specific draft revision and is not compatible with
+  other revisions or with other implementations that pin a different one.
+- No post-quantum signature algorithm is implemented. A P2MR leaf script can only use the opcodes
+  that BIP 342 already defines.
+- There is no wallet support: no descriptor, no address generation, no signing and no coin
+  selection. `IsMine` never matches a P2MR output.
+- P2MR is disabled on mainnet, testnet3, testnet4 and the public signet, and there is no mechanism
+  in this build to enable it there.
